.TH SCENE 1 "2026-08-24" "scene 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
scene \- fast, keyboard\-first Linux launcher
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B scene
.RB [ \-\-background ]
.RB [ \-\-measure ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B Scene
is a keyboard\-first launcher for Linux, built as one binary against native
GTK 4 and aimed at KDE Plasma on Wayland first. Activate it, type, and it ranks
installed applications, folders, links, calculations, package queries and its
own commands in one deterministic list.
.PP
Scene is a single\-instance application. Activating it while it is hidden
presents a focused launcher with a cleared query; activating it again hides the
same window. It never leaves a second launcher process or window behind.
.PP
System actions are typed and bounded rather than free\-form shell commands.
Search text is never interpreted as a command: a provider registers a fixed
program and argument vector, and nothing assembles one from what was typed.
Work that changes the system is confirmed first and escalates through
.BR pkexec (1),
so the desktop's own authorisation agent asks. Scene reports what it observed —
an unavailable tool, a permission failure, a timeout, a cancellation, or a
non\-zero exit — and distinguishes a program it watched finish from one it
started and handed over.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-background
Stay resident without presenting a window, so a global shortcut has a warm
process to activate. This is what the autostart entry Scene Settings installs
uses.
.TP
.B \-\-measure
Print this machine's startup, indexing, search\-latency and resident\-memory
figures and exit. A development tool: it runs its own process rather than
handing over to a resident Scene, so what it measures is a start. It presents
the window it is timing, so it needs a graphical session.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B Up, Down
Move the selection, wrapping at either end.
.TP
.B Enter
Run the selected result, or confirm a mutating action that asked first.
.TP
.B Escape
Clear the query; cancel a running action; withdraw a confirmation; on an empty
query, hide the launcher.
.TP
.B Ctrl+K
Open the selected result's other actions.
.TP
.B Ctrl+,
Open Scene Settings: shortcut and Copilot\-key status, providers, history and
autostart.
.TP
.B Ctrl+Q
Quit.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B SCENE_DIRECTORY
Directory the configured\-directory provider opens. Overrides the configured
value for one session and is never written back.
.TP
.B SCENE_HISTORY
Set to
.BR off ,
.BR 0 ,
.B no
or
.B false
to switch off the recent/frequent ranking adjustment for one session.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/scene/config.ini
Configuration: the configured directory, provider order and enable state, and
the history switches. Its
.B [format]
section names the version it was written in; Scene upgrades an older file at
startup and keeps the previous one beside it as
.IR config.ini.format\-N .
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/scene/history
What has been run, and when, for the recent/frequent ranking adjustment. Its
first line names its format version.
.TP
.I $XDG_CACHE_HOME/scene/eurofxref\-daily.xml
Cached European Central Bank reference rates for currency conversion.
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/autostart/dev.scene.Scene.desktop
Written and removed by Scene Settings when user\-level autostart is switched on
or off.
.SH NOTES
A Wayland client cannot place its own window. On KDE Plasma centring is a KWin
setting — System Settings, Window Management, Window Behavior, Advanced, Window
placement — rather than something Scene can assert, and Scene reports the limit
instead of simulating placement.
.PP
KDE owns the global shortcut. Scene's desktop entry proposes
.B Meta+Space
as a fallback and Scene reads the binding KDE actually recorded; it never writes
.IR kglobalshortcutsrc .
Starting
.B scene
from a shell gets no activation token, so its window opens behind others; the
global shortcut is the path that works.
.PP
The Copilot key is a
.B Shift+Super+F23
chord emitting
.BR XF86Assistant ,
which KDE's Qt\-based recorder cannot bind. Scene detects and reports what it
observes rather than promising support.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR pkexec (1),
.BR desktop\-file\-validate (1)
.PP
The product plan, the KRunner parity track and the packaging notes ship with the
source at
.UR https://github.com/fullstacktaiye/Scene
.UE .
